%% Evidence blackboard — how a source becomes a queryable knowledge graph.
%% The store is append-only SQLite under ~/.blackboard; writes are events, reads are
%% read-only SQL over projected tables (works, anchors, citations, claims, ...) and
%% the anchors_fts full-text index. Discovery (finding papers, resolving references
%% to DOIs) is the scholar engine's job, composed in at the marked steps.
%% Render with any Mermaid viewer, or read top-to-bottom as an ordered message log.
sequenceDiagram
    actor Driver as Claude (skill driver)
    participant Scholar as scholar engine (discovery)
    participant Board as blackboard package
    participant Store as SQLite (~/.blackboard)
    participant Datalab as Datalab (Marker) parser
    participant Enrich as Enrichment (LLM/VLM)

    Driver->>Scholar: search / fulltext / zotero_items
    Scholar-->>Driver: PDFs and DOIs
    Driver->>Board: add_source (binds the source to a canonical work)
    Board->>Store: append work + source events

    note over Driver,Enrich: ingest runs as a background bash command (slow, model/network-bound)
    Driver->>Board: ingest(board, source)
    Board->>Datalab: parse the document
    Datalab-->>Board: Marker block tree, stored verbatim
    Board->>Enrich: citation markers, figure descriptions, per-block aspect, bibliography split into entries
    Enrich-->>Board: derived facts (references left unresolved)
    Board->>Store: append aspect-tagged anchors, citations, bibliography, figures
    Board->>Store: quarantine any unreadable source
    Board-->>Driver: harness wakes the driver with the ingest result

    Driver->>Scholar: resolve each unresolved bibliography entry to a DOI
    Scholar-->>Driver: DOIs
    Driver->>Board: link_reference (attach cited work, close citation edges)
    Driver->>Board: add_claim + cite_evidence (facts backed by anchors across works)
    Driver->>Board: classify (tag works with topics)
    Board->>Store: append works, claim_support, work_topics

    Driver->>Board: query("SELECT ... FROM claims / citations / works / anchors_fts ...")
    Board->>Store: read-only SQL (SELECT/WITH only)
    Store-->>Board: rows
    Board-->>Driver: evidence and graph structure backing each claim
